146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (People have always known me as a good writer, but somehow, I can't find words worthy of you. I've lost more than a cousin; I've lost a brother, a best friend, and a piece of my childhood. We were so close that people often thought we were siblings, and honestly, that's exactly what we were in our own way. You were the older cousin brother, and I was the younger cousin sister who always looked up to you.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E ( I still remember hearing stories about you before we met, imagining you as the fearless Rambo from the movies, only to meet a little boy who would eventually become one of the most important people in my life. I'll never forget the day you came with your dad carrying that green bucket full of honey, wearing shorts just like mine. I wanted us to match so badly that I cried when I couldn't find mine. Little did I know that the boy I was so excited to meet would become my childhood, my companion, my teacher, and the brother I would forever cherish. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (You shaped the person I became in ways words could never fully explain. Now, I would give anything for one more ordinary day with you, one more laugh, one more conversation, and one more memory together. The hardest part of losing you is knowing that you've taken a piece of our childhood with you, a piece only we could understand. But I'll keep telling our story, Gram, because you deserve to be remembered.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
